        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ceftazidime is a third-generation cephalosporin antibiotic. Like other third-generation cephalosporins, it has broad spectrum activity against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. Unlike most third-generation agents, it is active against Pseudomonas aeruginosa, however it has weaker activity against Gram-positive microorganisms and is not used for such infections.</owl:annotatedTarget>
