        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The Verone integron-encoded metallo-beta-lactamase (VIM) family was reported from Italy in 1999. There are, to date, 23 reported variants.  VIM enzymes mostly occur in P. aeruginosa, also P. putida and, very rarely, Enterobacteriaceae. Integron-associated, sometimes within plasmids. Hydrolyses all beta-lactams except monobactams, and evades all beta-lactam inhibitors.  There is a strong incidence of these in East Asia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
