        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Diaminopyrimidines are a class of organic compounds containing a pyrimidine ring substituted by two amine groups.  They are inhibitors of dihydrofolate reductase, an enzyme critical for DNA synthesis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
