        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Gramicidin D is a mixture of the linear peptides gramicidin A, B, and C, each with 15 alternating L- and D-amino acids. They are active against most gram-positive bacteria and select gram-negative bacteria. These compounds create channels in the bacterial membrane and increase the permeability to cations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
