        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The mphA gene encodes for resistance enzyme MPH(2&apos;)-I which preferentially inactivate 14-membered macrolides (e.g.erythromycin, telithromycin, roxithromycin) over 16-membered macrolides (e.g.tylosin, spiramycin). It phosphorylates macrolides at 2&apos;-OH hydroxyl of desosamine sugar of macrolides in a GTP-dependent manner.</obo:IAO_0000115>
