        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The rho transcription terminator factor moves along RNA as it is transcribed, unwinding the RNA from the DNA. It is also responsible for recognizing transcription termination pause sites, slowing down RNA polymerase and allowing mRNA to be released.</owl:annotatedTarget>
