        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Topoisomerases are responsible for winding and relaxing supercoiled DNA. The subunits of gyrase (gyrA, gyrB) and topoisomerase IV (parC, parE, parY) are targeted by antibiotics.</obo:IAO_0000115>
