        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AAC(6&apos;)-Iy is a chromosomal-encoded aminoglycoside acetyltransferase in S. enteritidis and S. enterica. Regulatory mutation required to increase expression of this chromosomally-encoded gene for resistance. In the specific system, aminoglycoside resistance was due to a transcriptional fusion secondary to a chromosomal deletion in which the downstream aac(6&apos;)-Iy gene was placed under the control of the upstream nmpC promoter.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AAC(6&apos;)-Iy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
