        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Precursor molecule during the synthesis of bacterial cell wall. Lipid II anchors itself onto the cell and it&apos;s disaccharide-peptide subunit is used in PG polymer assembly by peptidoglycan glycosyltransferases. Due to it&apos;s importance in cell wall synthesis, it is the target of antibiotics.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">antibiotic_resistance</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
