        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">kasA is a ketoacyl acyl carrier protein synthase that catalyzes the condensation reaction of fatty acid synthesis by the addition to an acyl acceptor of two carbons from malonyl-ACP. It is involved in elongation of fatty acids intermediate in the biosynthetic pathway of mycolic acids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
