        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FusB encodes a 2-domain zinc-binding protein that binds the ribosomal translocase EF-G, causing it to dissociate from the ribosome. This action increases the ribosomal turnover rate and confers resistance to fusidic acid. This protein is considered a FusB-type protein.</owl:annotatedTarget>
