        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A ToxR negatively regulated outer membrane porin. In Vibrio cholerae, ToxR controls resistance to P2 (a BPI-derived antimicrobial peptide) by regulating the production of OmpT, especially in the absence of OmpU.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PMID:10632889</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
