        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">mecD is a PBP2a variant identified on a genomic resistance island in Macrococcus caseolyticus. MecD confers resistance to methicillin and other beta-lactam antibiotics through the production of an alternative low-affinity PBP. First described by Schwendener et al. 2017 and identified from canine and bovine sources.</owl:annotatedTarget>
