        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC), in microbiology, is the lowest concentration of an antimicrobial that will inhibit the visible growth of a microorganism after overnight incubation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
