        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Fisetin is a flavonoid produced mainly by plants in the Eudicotidae clade. It exhibits a range of biological activities such as anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties, and fisetin has been shown to inhibit the action of metallo-beta-lactamases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
